Open seat: Jared Golden (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Maine's second district is an open seat after Jared Golden's retirement, and it pairs a Republican-leaning electorate with a favorable national environment for Democrats. Former Secretary of State Matt Dunlap has led in most recent surveys, including a nonpartisan University of New Hampshire poll, though several of those polls were sponsored by Democratic groups. Former Governor Paul LePage has slightly more money in the bank and remains a well-known figure who has won statewide before, but he has faced sustained attacks over his part-time Florida residency and on Social Security.\n\nIndependent raters mostly call the race Lean Republican, while prediction markets disagree sharply, with one pricing LePage as the favorite and another favoring Dunlap. The result is a genuine tossup with only a slight edge to Dunlap on the strength of recent polling and the midterm climate. Turnout patterns in this rural, working-class district, and how undecided voters weigh LePage's familiarity against his liabilities, will likely decide it.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4353, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4338, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4042, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4713, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3776, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3456, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_d